WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.762
Here's what Microsoft gives you.

2
00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:05.799
The admin center can create an
extension and a new Logic App together.

3
00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:10.732
For an existing Logic App, Learn publishes
one workflow definition to paste in:

4
00:00:10.732 --> 00:00:14.374
a trigger that describes what
Lifecycle Workflows sends,

5
00:00:14.374 --> 00:00:18.850
one callback action, and a gap in the
middle labelled "add your logic here".

6
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.563
That's Microsoft's only sample; a
search found no template anywhere else.

7
00:00:23.563 --> 00:00:28.993
Because it lives only inside a web page,
the repository pins the page with checked

8
00:00:28.993 --> 00:00:34.099
hashes, and a tiny interpreter runs the
definition, unchanged, against fakes.

9
00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.860
So you see what it really does.
